#.vscode/

# Flutter/Dart/Pub related
**/doc/api/
**/ios/Flutter/.last_build_id
.dart_tool/
.flutter-plugins-dependencies
.pub-cache/
.pub/
/build/
/coverage/

# Symbolication related
app.*.symbols

# Obfuscation related
app.*.map.json

# Android Studio will place build artifacts here
/android/app/debug
/android/app/profile
/android/app/release

# ─── Secrets / credentials ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Never commit runtime secrets. See docs/SECURITY.md for the full
# rotation + history-scrub runbook.
#
# Local env file (loaded at runtime via flutter_dotenv)
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

# Template is committed (no real values)
!.env.example

# Firebase Admin SDK service account — full project admin access.
# Each developer must drop a copy of this file from their secure
# credentials store. functions/index.js loads it via `require`.
functions/service-account.json

# Firebase Android config — contains the Android API key. The Gradle
# plugin reads it from disk, so the file can live outside the repo.
android/app/google-services.json

# Build artefact that has been known to leak merged keys
/lib/firebase_options.dart.bak
